<p>History typically remembers the 1901 Pan American Expo only as the setting for the assination of US President William McKinley. The President addressed the attendees on September 5. He returned to the Exposition the following day. On September 6, President William McKinley was assassinated by Leon Czlgosa outside the Temple of Music. He died eight days later. Theodore Roosevelt was inaugurated President on September 14, 1901.</p>
